# Orthic incenter lemma — the altitude from A bisects the angle of the orthic triangle at its foot (the orthocenter is the orthic triangle's incenter) (source: Coxeter & Greitzer)
A B C = triangle
Fa = foot(A, line(B, C))
Fb = foot(B, line(C, A))
Fc = foot(C, line(A, B))
prove eqangle(Fa, Fb, Fa, A, Fa, A, Fa, Fc)
